<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nile Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> Valley is the narrow strip of fertile land along the River Nile through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, watered by its annual flood. It supported the civilisations of ancient Egypt and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> and the later states of Kush, the Christian Nubian kingdoms and the Funj. As the main corridor between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, it carried trade, armies and pilgrims for thousands of years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nile-valley.jpg" alt="Nile Valley" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fiktube · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
